-    "what_it_would_claim": "The NR4A3 5' fusion partner is a candidate - not established - treatment-stratification variable in EMC, and its two halves are in different states. On PROGNOSIS, pooling the two cohorts that publish event counts by partner (73 patients, two continents, no shared authors) gives a crude disease-specific death rate of 7/15 = 46.7% (95% CI 24.8-69.9) with TAF15::NR4A3 against 6/58 = 10.3% (4.8-20.8) with EWSR1::NR4A3 - a magnitude this contrast has never had - reported inseparably from the multivariable analysis in the larger of those cohorts, in which the partner is NOT independent of tumour size and 78% of TAF15 tumours exceed 10 cm, so the partner may be a marker for a big tumour rather than for a biology. On TREATMENT RESPONSE the record supports a DIRECTION and no magnitude at all, because the entire published TAF15::NR4A3 antiangiogenic-TKI experience is three to five patients with no reported responses and a 95% upper bound lying above the comparator arm's own point estimate; a zero-event arm yields no magnitude at any denominator, and nothing in the prognostic result bears on it. The review literature's metastasis claim is supported by neither count-bearing cohort in either direction. It makes no treatment recommendation and asserts no efficacy, safety, therapeutic window or clinical readiness for any agent.",
+    "what_it_would_claim": "A descriptive, explicitly selected accounting of what published EMC reports record about the NR4A3 5' fusion partner, with every denominator, source limit and conditioning assumption stated. It establishes the partner as a CANDIDATE - not established - stratification variable and makes no treatment recommendation. RESPONSE: the antiangiogenic-TKI evidence is a CONDITIONAL RECONSTRUCTION over 3 to 5 TAF15::NR4A3 patients with no recorded objective response - 0/3 versus 4/19 in the pazopanib trial NCT02066285, conditional on all three reported TAF15 patients sitting inside the 22 primary-endpoint-evaluable set, which no retained source establishes; and 0/5 versus 10/27 as a conditional descriptive mixture with the sunitinib named-use series, which additionally assumes distinct patients across two drugs and settings and inherits the evaluability assumption. The observed differences of recorded proportions (21.1 and 37.0 percentage points) exist; the population magnitudes they estimate are imprecise, with the TAF15 arm's 95% Wilson upper bound (43.4-56.1%) lying above the comparator's own point estimate; and A COMPARISON CONFINED TO TREATED PATIENTS CANNOT ESTABLISH THAT THE PARTNER MODIFIES TREATMENT BENEFIT AT ANY DENOMINATOR. OUTCOME: one series carries the main event analysis - Agaram 2014 records disease-specific death 3/7 with TAF15 against 1/16 with EWSR1, one further EWSR1 patient dead of unknown cause, local recurrence 2/7 against 1/16 and distant recurrence 2/7 against 6/16, over arms whose mean observation windows differ about two-fold - and a second series' per-partner counts are separately source-verified and reported beside it rather than pooled (Sjogren 2003: 0/3 TAF15 against 1/5 EWSR1 recorded tumour-related deaths). PREVALENCE: TAF15::NR4A3 is recorded in 28/154 = 18.2% (95% CI 12.9-25.0) of NAMED-PARTNER-ASSIGNED cases in four selected series - a conditional share among assigned cases, not an estimate for all EMC and not the size of any clinical population. The molecular-confirmation stage behind those denominators (26/58/12/67) is a DIFFERENT set of integers from the named-partner counts (24/57/11/62). WITHDRAWN 2026-09-08, and this entry previously asserted all of them: the two-cohort 73-patient pooled prognostic magnitude (7/15 versus 6/58) - its Huang 2023 Table 1 inputs are not verified by any retained original and are quarantined, which is scoped absence and not a finding that the published counts are wrong; the proposition that a zero-event arm yields no magnitude at any denominator, which is mathematically false; the size-versus-biology explanation of the death excess; the claim to cover the entire published experience or to combine literatures nobody had combined, which no systematic search supports and which prior reviews contradict; and the refutation of the 2020 review's cautious metastasis-free-survival trend, a different endpoint that a non-significant crude tally cannot refute. SOURCE LIMITS: no systematic search was run, so nothing here is a census; the response denominators rest on secondary provenance and no primary full text of either TKI report is held; the comparator arms are labelled non-TAF15 and no comparison against a trial-level verified EWSR1 arm exists anywhere in this synthesis; the reported prognostic analyses do not establish an independent partner effect IN EITHER DIRECTION, and no event count, coefficient or model specification is available to assess them; no signed direction of follow-up, selection or missingness bias is claimed; and no time-to-event quantity, hazard ratio or individual prognosis is derived. It asserts no efficacy, safety, selectivity, therapeutic window or clinical readiness for any agent, in any patient group, at any line of therapy, and no wet-lab work was performed.",
